WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.467
-[ Grunts ]

00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:03.634
[ Weapon whirs ]

00:00:03.634 --> 00:00:04.667
-Ahh!

00:00:04.667 --> 00:00:06.567
-Okay, I have a suit.

00:00:06.567 --> 00:00:08.767
-Yeah, I noticed.

00:00:08.767 --> 00:00:11.601
You okay?
-Yes!

00:00:11.601 --> 00:00:13.667
-Look, momentum, right?

00:00:13.667 --> 00:00:14.901
Jump, tap, right?

00:00:14.901 --> 00:00:16.834
One move. Jump-tap.
-I know how to do it, Dad!

00:00:16.834 --> 00:00:18.033
-Oh, do you?
-Yes!

00:00:18.033 --> 00:00:19.667
-Really? 'Cause it didn't
look like it from my end.

00:00:19.667 --> 00:00:20.834
-I messed up on the timing.

00:00:20.834 --> 00:00:22.701
-Jump -- Ahh.

00:00:22.701 --> 00:00:24.234
Ahh!

00:00:24.234 --> 00:00:25.634
-Oh!

00:00:25.634 --> 00:00:27.534
-[ Grunts ]

00:00:27.534 --> 00:00:29.901
-Like that. You see what I did?
You see what I did?

00:00:29.901 --> 00:00:31.033
-No.

00:00:31.033 --> 00:00:32.367
You're like, this small.

00:00:32.367 --> 00:00:34.067
-I jumped and tapped!

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:35.434
-Welcome back to "Late Night"!

00:00:35.434 --> 00:00:36.667
We're here with Paul Rudd!

00:00:36.667 --> 00:00:38.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:41.000
That was a clip from "Ant-Man
and the Wasp: Quantumania,"

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:42.701
a very anticipated film.

00:00:42.701 --> 00:00:44.434
-I don't know if this is
true or not.

00:00:44.434 --> 00:00:47.133
Somehow, I heard word that

00:00:47.133 --> 00:00:49.734
Schumaker was somehow able
to get tickets

00:00:49.734 --> 00:00:53.634
on Thursday night.
-Yeah!

00:00:53.634 --> 00:00:56.234
-Who does he know?
-Yeah!

00:00:56.234 --> 00:00:57.400
He's been walking around --

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:00.300
I guess he knows this
Jeff Fandango guy.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:01.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.300
-He must be high up.
-Hollywood bigwig.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:06.234
High up the Marvel chain.

00:01:06.234 --> 00:01:07.367
-That's impressive.

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:09.434
-This is really fun.
Third movie.

00:01:09.434 --> 00:01:11.200
-Third one.
-Third one of the Ant-Man.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:14.067
And this one's a really fun
dynamic of teenage daughter,

00:01:14.067 --> 00:01:16.534
which you have now.
-Mm-hmm. Yep.

00:01:16.534 --> 00:01:19.534
-How have you found being a
parent of a teenage daughter?

00:01:19.534 --> 00:01:21.000
Are you enjoying that journey?

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.000
I know it's the front end
of being a teenager.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.367
-It's great.
-Yeah?

00:01:24.367 --> 00:01:27.534
-My daughter, she's just now
starting to approach that,

00:01:27.534 --> 00:01:31.234
and I'm a little nervous.

00:01:31.234 --> 00:01:34.133
People always say,
"Oh, teenage daughters.

00:01:34.133 --> 00:01:38.400
There's a few years there where
it can be a little challenging."

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:43.667
And it hasn't been yet, but --
-She hasn't turned on you yet?

00:01:43.667 --> 00:01:46.934
-Interview me in "Ant-Man 4."
-Yeah, okay. Got you.

00:01:46.934 --> 00:01:49.667
-Not that there is one,
by the way.

00:01:49.667 --> 00:01:51.167
Just, yeah.

00:01:51.167 --> 00:01:54.534
It just seemed like that was
the right joke to say for the --

00:01:54.534 --> 00:01:56.767
-But now everybody
at Marvel right now is

00:01:56.767 --> 00:01:58.968
pulling their hair out.
-Yeah, that's right.

00:01:58.968 --> 00:02:01.434
-"We told him not to
even talk about it!"

00:02:01.434 --> 00:02:03.601
-But on "Ant-Man 7,"
I'm gonna say,

00:02:03.601 --> 00:02:07.133
"She's the best.
She's so accepting.

00:02:07.133 --> 00:02:09.567
And she became a real friend.

00:02:09.567 --> 00:02:10.968
And open, and..."

00:02:10.968 --> 00:02:12.100
-And "Ant-Man 10,"
where you're like,

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:13.567
"And now she has a daughter!"

00:02:13.567 --> 00:02:16.300
-I know, it's so crazy.
It's so nuts.

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:19.334
You know, being a grandfather
is really something special.

00:02:19.334 --> 00:02:21.567
A little harder to
get into the suit,

00:02:21.567 --> 00:02:23.667
but we're managing!
-There you go.

00:02:23.667 --> 00:02:25.634
Now I know, and we've
talked about this before.

00:02:25.634 --> 00:02:28.200
First of all, it's always
so great to have you here.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:31.567
Oftentimes, I sort of am
lucky enough to have you,

00:02:31.567 --> 00:02:33.968
but it's the end of your
press tour, and I get it.

00:02:33.968 --> 00:02:35.534
You're sort of exhausted about
talking about this movie.

00:02:35.534 --> 00:02:36.734
There's probably no more

00:02:36.734 --> 00:02:38.434
anecdotes from the set
to share.

00:02:38.434 --> 00:02:39.601
-It's a tricky thing, you know?

00:02:39.601 --> 00:02:41.767
You want to, "Oh,
what's been going on?

00:02:41.767 --> 00:02:43.367
Are there any funny stories
or anything?"

00:02:43.367 --> 00:02:44.801
And you get a little
kind of tired.

00:02:44.801 --> 00:02:46.467
And there's only so --

00:02:46.467 --> 00:02:48.400
-Right, it wasn't like every day
there were hijinks.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:49.901
-The well gets dry.
-Yeah.

00:02:49.901 --> 00:02:52.434
So as a favor to you,

00:02:52.434 --> 00:02:54.067
I would like you to
tell us a story

00:02:54.067 --> 00:02:55.334
about something
that didn't happen.

00:02:55.334 --> 00:02:56.667
-Okay.

00:02:56.667 --> 00:02:58.667
-Just to give you a break,
right?

00:02:58.667 --> 00:03:00.634
-An anecdote, something that
just didn't happen to me?

00:03:00.634 --> 00:03:03.667
-Do you want me to just make up
the top of it for you?

00:03:03.667 --> 00:03:05.133
-Yeah, sure.
-Okay, great.

00:03:05.133 --> 00:03:08.434
-Oh, this is my favorite
kind of water, by the way.

00:03:08.434 --> 00:03:09.834
-Yeah?

00:03:09.834 --> 00:03:11.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.601 --> 00:03:13.801
Well, we had a regular size,

00:03:13.801 --> 00:03:15.868
but then we heard you wanted to
tie it into Ant-Man.

00:03:15.868 --> 00:03:18.334
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.334 --> 00:03:19.701
-That's right. Yeah.

00:03:19.701 --> 00:03:21.767
[ Applause ]

00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:23.234
You're the best, man.
-No

00:03:23.234 --> 00:03:24.467
-You are the best.

00:03:24.467 --> 00:03:27.234
I will do tie-ins!

00:03:27.234 --> 00:03:30.968
-Hold on, I'm gonna chug it.

00:03:30.968 --> 00:03:33.868
[ Cheering ]

00:03:33.868 --> 00:03:35.534
-Wow.

00:03:35.534 --> 00:03:37.167
[ Applause ]

00:03:37.167 --> 00:03:38.868
[ Crunches ]
-Oh.

00:03:38.868 --> 00:03:40.400
[ Crunch ]

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:41.767
[ Empty bottle thuds ]

00:03:41.767 --> 00:03:43.200
Alright.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:45.033
-So you don't mind?
-No, whatever you want.

00:03:45.033 --> 00:03:47.734
-I will say the kind of story
that I would like you

00:03:47.734 --> 00:03:48.934
to be coming here to tell.
-Okay.

00:03:48.934 --> 00:03:51.334
-So I heard you were skiing
in Switzerland,

00:03:51.334 --> 00:03:52.734
and you were on one of
those gondolas.

00:03:52.734 --> 00:03:54.434
-Yeah.
-And it stopped halfway up

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:57.634
and you were stuck on it
with 11 strangers for 24 hours.

00:03:57.634 --> 00:03:59.667
-It was the craziest thing.

00:03:59.667 --> 00:04:01.667
Also it was the first time
I'd ever been there.

00:04:01.667 --> 00:04:03.834
I'm nervous about heights
anyway.
-Sure.

00:04:03.834 --> 00:04:07.367
-And the few times that
I'd taken the ski --

00:04:07.367 --> 00:04:08.734
It was the two-seater, you know?

00:04:08.734 --> 00:04:10.534
Like, the standard. I hate it.

00:04:10.534 --> 00:04:12.133
But the great thing about being
in Switzerland, in the Alps,

00:04:12.133 --> 00:04:13.534
they have the gondolas.
-Yeah.

00:04:13.534 --> 00:04:15.434
Nice and warm,
protected from the elements.

00:04:15.434 --> 00:04:17.234
-Warm, protected.

00:04:17.234 --> 00:04:20.501
The thing is,
is when you are in there

00:04:20.501 --> 00:04:22.968
with all of those people
and it stops,

00:04:22.968 --> 00:04:24.100
they're from different
parts of the world.

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:25.367
I was the only one
who spoke English.

00:04:25.367 --> 00:04:26.501
-Oh, God.

00:04:26.501 --> 00:04:28.934
-Yeah! And...

00:04:28.934 --> 00:04:30.167
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.167 --> 00:04:34.968
And power goes out, everything,
it shut down,

00:04:34.968 --> 00:04:37.133
and there was no way that
we were gonna get down,

00:04:37.133 --> 00:04:38.367
and I was really panicked.

00:04:38.367 --> 00:04:40.734
And so I started asking people,
"What do we do?"

00:04:40.734 --> 00:04:44.300
And no one could talk to me.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:47.167
-Did you feel like any of them
even recognized you?

00:04:47.167 --> 00:04:50.267
Because again, your movies
are internationally known.

00:04:50.267 --> 00:04:52.434
Did you feel any recognition?

00:04:52.434 --> 00:04:54.200
-No, not at all.

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:56.033
[ Laughter ]
There was one person,

00:04:56.033 --> 00:04:58.367
one person who did recognize me.

00:04:58.367 --> 00:05:00.300
But they were
ultimately disappointed,

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:02.734
because they actually pegged me
for being a writer on your show.

00:05:02.734 --> 00:05:04.667
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, right.

00:05:04.667 --> 00:05:07.234
[ Applause ]

00:05:10.334 --> 00:05:12.267
-All the way around.
-Wow, wow.

00:05:12.267 --> 00:05:14.200
-All the way around.
-Right. Oh, wow.

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:15.601
-Yeah.
-See, that was a great story.

00:05:15.601 --> 00:05:18.968
-It got a little slow
in the middle.

00:05:18.968 --> 00:05:21.734
-But I think when you can
pay it off like that --

00:05:21.734 --> 00:05:24.534
Don't be hard --
When you get worried

00:05:24.534 --> 00:05:26.200
about not having stories
on talk shows,

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:28.400
just ask for the ol' set-up.
-Yeah. That's just it.

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:31.133
You throw anything,
it's a much better way to go.

00:05:31.133 --> 00:05:33.067
Did I tell you about the time
I was scuba diving

00:05:33.067 --> 00:05:35.400
in Cozumel?

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:37.367
-And so just real quick
before you tell me,

00:05:37.367 --> 00:05:38.968
happened or didn't happen?
-Didn't happen.

00:05:38.968 --> 00:05:40.567
-Tell me.

00:05:40.567 --> 00:05:43.868
-Well, apparently --
I'm new to scuba diving.

00:05:43.868 --> 00:05:45.968
You're not supposed to fly
the next day.

00:05:45.968 --> 00:05:48.701
-Oh, gotcha.
-Also, when you go below

00:05:48.701 --> 00:05:50.701
60 feet or something,
you have to kind of

00:05:50.701 --> 00:05:52.000
decompress for three minutes.

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:54.300
You get something called,
I think, nitrogen narcosis.

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:55.467
Something like that.

00:05:55.467 --> 00:05:56.701
And then I you fly
the next day,

00:05:56.701 --> 00:05:58.234
you can get the bends.
you can die.

00:05:58.234 --> 00:05:59.767
-Oh, okay.

00:05:59.767 --> 00:06:01.667
-I came this close...

00:06:01.667 --> 00:06:03.501
[ Laughter ]

00:06:03.501 --> 00:06:05.868
...to getting an early flight
out of Cozumel.

00:06:05.868 --> 00:06:07.267
-Wow!

00:06:07.267 --> 00:06:08.634
And you think you full-on
would have died

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:09.701
if you got on it?

00:06:09.701 --> 00:06:11.234
-I know I would have died.
-Wow!

00:06:11.234 --> 00:06:12.601
[ Laughter ]

00:06:12.601 --> 00:06:15.267
-I know I would have died.
-Talk about a dodged bullet!

00:06:15.267 --> 00:06:16.934
-Oh, my God.

00:06:16.934 --> 00:06:19.033
And it was only because
the flight --

00:06:19.033 --> 00:06:21.567
we were there and there was
an issue with the plane,

00:06:21.567 --> 00:06:22.901
so I had to wait a whole day.

00:06:22.901 --> 00:06:25.634
It was Mexico.
There's not a lot of flights.

00:06:25.634 --> 00:06:26.934
So I had to wait.

00:06:26.934 --> 00:06:28.467
-And now is it true
that you actually

00:06:28.467 --> 00:06:30.167
made a big scene about the fact

00:06:30.167 --> 00:06:31.267
that there was a problem
with the plane?

00:06:31.267 --> 00:06:32.300
You were like,
"Do you know who I am?"

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:34.667
-That's exactly right.

00:06:34.667 --> 00:06:36.601
-And in reality, though,
you didn't realize at the time

00:06:36.601 --> 00:06:37.701
your life was being saved.

00:06:37.701 --> 00:06:39.234
-Had no clue.
-Wow!

00:06:39.234 --> 00:06:40.434
-None whatsoever.

00:06:40.434 --> 00:06:42.968
But I had to get back.
I knew I had to get back.

00:06:42.968 --> 00:06:44.267
You know why?
-Why?

00:06:44.267 --> 00:06:47.667
-It was the championship game
Chiefs vs. Bengals,

00:06:47.667 --> 00:06:49.534
and I'm like,
"I can't be late to this!

00:06:49.534 --> 00:06:51.334
My son will never forgive me!"

00:06:51.334 --> 00:06:52.501
-Right!

00:06:52.501 --> 00:06:54.634
But meanwhile,
he's lucky you did,

00:06:54.634 --> 00:06:56.634
'cause otherwise, he'd be
at the Super Bowl alone

00:06:56.634 --> 00:06:58.334
'cause his dad, dead in the air.

00:06:58.334 --> 00:07:00.234
[ Laughter ]

00:07:00.234 --> 00:07:02.601
-Yeah.
-What a crazy story.

00:07:02.601 --> 00:07:05.133
-All things work out the way
they're supposed to work out.

00:07:05.133 --> 00:07:06.734
Yeah, yeah.

00:07:06.734 --> 00:07:09.200
And by the way,
the diving was phenomenal.

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:10.234
-Oh, great.

00:07:10.234 --> 00:07:11.601
[ Laughter ]

00:07:11.601 --> 00:07:15.701
-Real quick, three favorite
things you saw underwater.

00:07:15.701 --> 00:07:17.734
-My three favorite things I saw?

00:07:17.734 --> 00:07:20.434
-I know you're 60 feet
or more at this point,

00:07:20.434 --> 00:07:22.234
but what are the three
favorite things you saw?

00:07:22.234 --> 00:07:23.734
-Parrotfish.
-Okay.

00:07:23.734 --> 00:07:25.467
[ Laughter ]

00:07:25.467 --> 00:07:28.834
-I saw an eel, which by the way,
you think, oh --

00:07:28.834 --> 00:07:31.300
They're very hard to see,
but I was able.

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:32.834
I was over a bit of a reef,

00:07:32.834 --> 00:07:36.100
and I did get to see
a moray eel.

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:38.334
-Okay. They're hard to see
because they move so fast?

00:07:38.334 --> 00:07:41.467
-No, they don't like to be seen.
-Okay, gotcha.

00:07:41.467 --> 00:07:43.100
[ Laughter ]

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:45.634
-And then
-So parrotfish, moray eel.

00:07:45.634 --> 00:07:46.667
-Parrotfish, moray eel,

00:07:46.667 --> 00:07:48.067
and then just a body.

00:07:48.067 --> 00:07:50.067
I don't know, it was just,
like, floating.

00:07:50.067 --> 00:07:51.100
[ Laughter ]

00:07:51.100 --> 00:07:52.367
I don't know what happened.

00:07:52.367 --> 00:07:54.367
I didn't follow up on it.

00:07:54.367 --> 00:07:55.734
-Now, that's interesting.

00:07:55.734 --> 00:07:57.734
Did you tell, or were you sort
of like, you know what?

00:07:57.734 --> 00:07:59.501
-I was too freaked out.
I didn't say a word.

00:07:59.501 --> 00:08:02.634
I was like, "Oh, my God.
There's just a dead body."

00:08:04.067 --> 00:08:07.234
Maybe it went deeper
than 60 feet,

00:08:07.234 --> 00:08:08.868
didn't take the time,
and then...

00:08:08.868 --> 00:08:10.234
-Didn't take the class.

00:08:10.234 --> 00:08:12.501
Everybody has to take the class
before they go diving,

00:08:12.501 --> 00:08:13.767
and that guy was like,
"I'm fine."

00:08:13.767 --> 00:08:15.767
"I'm fine. I got it.
You can breathe. I get it.

00:08:15.767 --> 00:08:16.868
I'll use this.

00:08:16.868 --> 00:08:18.267
I'll go up, I'll be able
to breathe again."

00:08:18.267 --> 00:08:21.167
Nitrogen narcosis
knocked him out.

00:08:21.167 --> 00:08:22.501
-Wow.
-Yeah.

00:08:22.501 --> 00:08:23.634
-What a cool -- I mean, again,

00:08:23.634 --> 00:08:24.901
obviously not a story
he can tell,

00:08:24.901 --> 00:08:26.868
but pretty cool that Paul Rudd
was who found him.

00:08:26.868 --> 00:08:28.367
-He'll never know.
-Yeah.

00:08:28.367 --> 00:08:30.000
[ Laughter ]

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.200
Thank you so much for sharing

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:32.300
these things that
never happened.

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:33.567
-I've never talked about this
before!

00:08:33.567 --> 00:08:34.634
-It's wonderful.

00:08:34.634 --> 00:08:36.634
You guys, that's Paul Rudd!

00:08:36.634 --> 00:08:37.801
There's nobody better.

00:08:37.801 --> 00:08:40.033
"Ant-Man and the Wasp:
Quantumania"

00:08:40.033 --> 00:08:42.334
premieres in theaters and IMAX
February 17th.

00:08:42.334 --> 00:08:44.067
We'll be right back
with Popsicle Schtick.

00:08:44.067 --> 00:08:45.133
-I love Popsicle Schtick!

